course: dictionary
lesson: 8560
title: Scarce: not enough to go round
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scarce means there is not enough of something, or very little of it is available. Look at the words around it for clues. «Water is scarce in the desert.» Deserts are hot and dry, so the clue is that water is hard to get. Scarce means there is not enough.
explain: Scarce can also mean rare and hard to find. «Food like insects, fruit and fresh leaves becomes scarce in winter, though seeds and nuts can still be found.» The word though is the clue: some food is still there, but the good food is hard to find.
explain: Watch out for «make yourself scarce». This does not mean small or thin. It means go away quickly or keep out of the way. Test it by putting your meaning into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Scarce means there is not enough of something, or very little is available.
fact: «Scarce» can also mean rare and hard to find.
fact: «Make yourself scarce» means go away quickly or keep out of the way.
fact: Scarce resources, like water and food, are important in geography and science lessons.
fact: «Scarcely» is a related word, as in «I could scarcely hear her», and it is used like an adverb.
exercise: «Water is scarce in the desert.» What does scarce mean here? | It is very salty | *There is not enough of it | It is cold and wet | There is far too much of it
exercise: «Food becomes scarce in winter, though seeds and nuts can still be found.» Which word tells you that some food is still there? | Food | *Though | Scarce | Winter
exercise: Ben says, «Make yourself scarce before Mum sees the mess.» What does he mean? | *Go away quickly, and keep out of the way | Stand very still and quiet | Clean the room as quickly as you can | Hide the mess under the bed
test: «Bats fly out at sunset because food is scarce in the dark.» What does scarce mean here? | Very cold | Noisy | *Not enough, and hard to find | Bright and sunny
test: Which phrase means go away quickly or keep out of the way? | Scarcely any | *Make yourself scarce | Scarce resources | Food is scarce
exam: Which sentence uses scarce to mean rare and hard to find? | «He scarcely ate his dinner.» | «Make yourself scarce before the teacher comes.» | *«Good tickets are scarce, so book early.» | «Water is scarce in the desert.»
